libvterm vendoring
=================

Source: https://bazaar.leonerd.org.uk/c/libvterm/
Bazaar revision: 847 (2026-10-29)
Revision ID: leonerd@leonerd.org.uk-20261029213117-ufuqbcpo9edo3vqg
Release base: 0.3.3 (Bazaar revision 839)

This copy includes upstream revisions 840-847: pre-move and continuation-aware
scrollback callbacks, reflow cleanup, and bounds checking for excess CSI
parameters and subparameters. Upstream still
reports version 0.3.3; the Bazaar revision above identifies the snapshot.

To retrieve the pinned source:

    bzr export -r 847 /tmp/libvterm-r847 http://bazaar.leonerd.org.uk/c/libvterm/

Merge future upstream changes against this revision rather than replacing the
directory. Local changes include keyboard handling, parser bounds and escape
handling, glyph clusters and generated Unicode/emoji data, resize/reflow fixes,
BiDi support, and inline-image state and screen callbacks. The Makefile and
vterm.pc.in retain their release-tarball form, and only the existing source/test
subset is vendored. CMake builds the library and JNI wrapper for Android/host.

Compatibility exception: revision 845's change to bold/highbright handling is
reverted locally. termlib's boldAsBright option must continue promoting indexed
colours 0-7 when bold is applied, including Kismet's indexed black-on-black text.
The upstream SGR 38 test is adjusted to capture this existing behaviour; the
ShellIntegrationTest Kismet regression also covers it through JNI.

Validation:

    make -C lib/src/main/cpp/libvterm test
    ./gradlew :lib:testDebugUnitTest --no-configuration-cache
